# Replicon WCF API Integration Guide

## 1. The Core Engine: `wcfRequest`

This is your custom wrapper function for every POST request to Replicon.

**How to use it:**

```javascript

await wcfRequest(
    "Step Description for Logs", 
    "https://ap1.replicon.com/{company}/services/{ServiceName}.svc/{MethodName}", 
    { payloadObject }, 
    headers
);

```

**Why we built it this way:**
Replicon's WCF endpoints throw very obscure 500 and 400 errors if a single field is missing. The `wcfRequest` function uses a `try/catch` block to intercept the Axios error, dig into `error.response.data`, and print the exact XML/JSON rejection string from the server directly into your Docker logs. Always use this instead of native `axios.post` for WCF calls.

